From d79fb3b4f281cf582675defba35e31e12d429e45 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BaresipKit <baresipkit@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 22:43:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ice: support ICE restart

Add an optional restart hook to struct mnat and call_restart_mnat().
call_reset_transp() uses the hook when the media NAT supports it. The
ICE module creates new credentials; when the local address changed or
a TURN connection was lost it drops its STUN/TURN state, gathers again
and re-INVITEs once gathering completes, otherwise it keeps the
gathered candidates and TURN allocations (a new allocation from the
same 5-tuple would be rejected) and re-INVITEs right away. Connectivity
checks start when the answer carries the peer's new credentials, and
are repeated a few times if they fail, since a peer may still answer
with 401 while it switches to its new credentials. A remote offer with
a new ice-ufrag restarts ICE on the answering side with the gathered
candidates, so the answer is complete.

A restart that cannot gather, or that gets no new credentials from the
peer within 15 seconds, emits the "failed" event and keeps the call, so
that it can be restarted again. The STUN/TURN server is not resolved
again.
---
 include/baresip.h |   4 +
 modules/ice/ice.c | 511 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---
 src/call.c        |  25 +++
 3 files changed, 516 insertions(+), 24 deletions(-)

